questions.explanation:
**Given**

**Find the relation**

100 → 1000

100 = 10&sup2;

1000 = 10&sup3;

So, the pattern is:

If a number is a perfect square (n&sup2;), it is converted to n&sup3;.

**Apply same logic to 64**

64 = 8&sup2;

So, 64 → 8&sup3;

= 512

Hence, the correct option is **Option 3.**

